# Citation metadata (Citation File Format). GitHub renders this as a "Cite this
# repository" button; Zenodo and Zotero read it too. Mirrors the citation block
# on /about/team — keep the two in sync.
# When a DOI is minted (Nakala or Zenodo), add:  doi: 10.xxxx/xxxxx
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reuse data or the platform in a publication, please cite it as below. Individual records carry their own attribution — cite the depositing laboratory alongside the platform."
title: "ManuSpectrum: a platform for the physicochemical analysis of written heritage"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Michelin
    given-names: Anne
    affiliation: "Centre de Recherche sur la Conservation (CRC), MNHN"
  - family-names: Kagan
    given-names: Gilles
    affiliation: "IRHT, CNRS"
  - family-names: Humeau
    given-names: Maxime
    affiliation: "Centre de Recherche sur la Conservation (CRC), MNHN"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CRC-Centre-Recherche-Conservation/ManuSpectrum"
license: GPL-3.0
keywords:
  - heritage science
  - conservation science
  - physicochemical analysis
  - manuscripts
  - written cultural heritage
  - spectroscopy
  - XRF
  - IIIF
  - CIDOC-CRM
  - Arches
abstract: "Interoperable database for the physicochemical analysis of written cultural heritage (manuscripts, printed books, inscriptions): XRF, Raman, FTIR, FORS and imaging data, structured with CIDOC-CRM/CRMsci and published through IIIF. A Biblissima+ Cluster 2 project (ANR-21-ESRE-0005) at the Centre de Recherche sur la Conservation (CRC), in partnership with Huma-Num."
